  "detail": "Five of the six earlier findings are fixed: narrow Cargo, rustup and bun allowances with credentials denied, relocated stores denied, a per-config policy, the specific re-deny test, and the two fixtures. The gate-profile blocker is still open. The orchestrator ran this PR's `runGates` on a recorded worktree under the real home, inside `readPolicyScope.run(loadConfig().readPolicy, ...)`. Setup, lint and typecheck passed, and the test check failed after 1,079 s. Every visible failure carried `Cannot resolve read policy path <home>/.rustup/toolchains`:\n- \"an unavailable pinned implementer stops with its chain and reason: quota|rejected\";\n- \"pinned verifier exhaustion redacts private holdout details: unavailable|rejected\";\n- \"audit allowances > engine audit honors persisted allowances: no opt-in|inline mention\";\n- \"audit allowances > private-string audit events and retry feedback redact filenames and values\";\n- \"a changes verdict runs one round that pushes onto the PR branch with the findings quoted\".\n\nThis PR's own real-Seatbelt regression, test/sandbox.test.ts:818 \"failure-injection outcomes survive a gate checkout under home\", also fails unconfined with the same error. Cause: inside a gate, the home directory is read-denied, so the strict component resolver gets EPERM from `realpathSync` (and `lstatSync`) on an absent optional path such as `~/.rustup/toolchains`, instead of ENOENT, and refuses. Tests that build factories and gates run nested inside the gate, so after a deploy every gate of this repository would fail.\n\nFix:\n- Separate required roots (checkout, scratch, Git paths) from optional toolchain candidates (bun, cargo and rustup subpaths, `toolchain_paths`).\n- In the component resolver, call `lstatSync(next, { throwIfNoEntry: false })` before `realpathSync(next)`, and don't realpath a component proven absent.\n- Treat an optional candidate as absent, and omit it from the allowances, when it doesn't exist, or when its existence can't be inspected because a denied ancestor blocks it (EPERM or EACCES from lstat on a path under the denied home). An optional allowance for a path that can't be seen grants nothing anyway.\n- Keep refusing for required roots that can't be resolved, for an existing entry (including a dangling symlink) that can't resolve, and for any overlap with a credential path, even for absent descendants.\n- Don't use `existsSync()` or catch-all exception handling to classify absence.\n\nTests, since real Seatbelt doesn't run in factory gates or CI: make the resolver's `lstatSync` and `realpathSync` injectable, and add non-skipped tests.\n- With lstat and realpath throwing EPERM for every path under a temporary home (as inside a confined gate) and no `.rustup`, `.cargo` or `.bun` present, the gate policy computes without throwing and omits those allowances.\n- A required root under the same conditions still refuses.\n- An existing dangling symlink candidate still refuses.\n\nKeep test/sandbox.test.ts:818 as the real-Seatbelt regression; the orchestrator will run it and the full suite under the profile unconfined."
